{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Do not look behind you.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: you shared in their wickedness, and by the merit of Abraham you are being saved; you are not entitled to gaze upon their punishment." "<b>And the Ramban,</b> of blessed memory, gave a reason for it: they were prevented from looking because gazing at the air in a place where the thing is there causes great harm and afflicts him. And so with all other contagious diseases — gazing causes great harm and afflicts them, and likewise thought concerning them, as is known from the bites of animals. For the bite of a mad dog: one sees in its urine the likeness of small pups, and if you pass that water through a sieve they are not seen there at all; wait until the end of an hour and they will be seen there as at first." "<b>And it is known</b> that one who has this illness does not drink any beverage at all, and if perchance he sees any beverage he suffers greatly and the likeness of the mad dog that bit him appears to him." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> 'Do not look behind you' — He said to them, do not look behind you, for the Shekhinah of the Holy One, blessed be He, had descended to rain upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire. Irit the wife of Lot — her compassion was stirred for her daughters who were married in Sodom, and she looked behind her to see whether they were following after them, and she beheld the Shekhinah behind her and became a pillar of salt."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:40.703426580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}